  "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-0.18<Z<0.18).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/061aec33cb30172ec64c89841fc70cb2e5bec9b89f92ef0427ff9673bfa99219.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=\u03a6(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $\u03a6(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.18<Z<0.18) & =P(Z<0.18)-P(Z\\le -0.18) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.18)-P(Z\\le -0.18) \\\\  & =\u03a6(0.18)-\u03a6(-0.18)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\n\u03a6(-0.18)=0.4286,\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $\u03a6(0.18).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(0.18) & =P(Z\\le 0.18) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge -0.18) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-0.18) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le -0.18) \\\\  & =1-\u03a6(-0.18) \\\\  & =1-0.4286 \\\\  & =0.5714\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.18<Z<0.18) & =\u03a6(0.18)-\u03a6(-0.18) \\\\  & =0.5714-0.4286 \\\\  & =0.1428.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
